#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# norlund_b

#% text
# `norlund_b(n, a)` gives the Norlund number, `n!` times the coefficient of `t^n` in `(t/(e^t - 1))^a`; `norlund_b(n, a, x)` gives the Norlund polynomial.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The result is a polynomial in `a` (and `x`); with `a = 1` it is the Bernoulli number `B_n`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
norlund_b(3, a)
#% output
#= (1/8)*a^2 - (1/8)*a^3

#% cell
norlund_b(4, 1)
#% output
#= -1/30

#% cell
norlund_b(2, a, x)
#% output
#= (-1/12)*a + (1/4)*a^2 - a*x + x^2

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `bernoulli_b`
